From 38c9d766f3d09b964f29493622be525e7c07974f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Cheng <chengyuejia@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:28:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Feature][Quantization] Align upstream experts_int8 with NPU
 INT8 cube

Upstream experts_int8 quantization only supports the TRITON MoE backend,
which does not run on Ascend NPU. Add AscendW8A8OnlineFusedMoEMethod that
loads fp16/bf16 expert weights and quantizes them per-row to int8 during
process_weights_after_loading, then reuses the W8A8_DYNAMIC MoE path so
execution dispatches to the NPU INT8 cube unit
(npu_grouped_matmul_swiglu_quant). Linear layers are left unquantized,
matching upstream semantics.

A platform patch overrides ExpertsInt8Config.get_quant_method to route
FusedMoE layers to the new scheme, so --quantization experts_int8 works
out of the box on NPU. Unit tests cover scheme registration, weight
loading dtype, per-row quantization correctness, post-loading weight
swap, and the patch routing behavior.

Co-authored-by: GLM-5.2
